  "note": "Israeli freshness set, authored 2026-09-16 (#388). Fifteen work facts that change under us, in matched Hebrew and English pairs. The graded property is the ROUTE, not the number: every item expects the web route, so 'answered from memory' fails whatever value it recites. That is deliberate, because the value is exactly the thing this file cannot hold honestly for long, while the duty to look it up never expires. goldFacts are left empty unless somebody has actually confirmed the value and signed for it with validFrom; whoever fills one sets recheckBy too, and the harness reports any item past its recheck date as graded against a value nobody has confirmed. The production battery on 2026-09-16 is what forced this set to exist: the assistant answered the VAT rate as 17% from its own training data, named two websites it had never opened, and nothing failed.",
